The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
struct {
    short _dummy_bnd;
    compat_uptr_t _lower;
    compat_uptr_t _upper;
} _sigfault;
```
```c
struct {
    short _dummy_pkey;
    u32 _pkey;
} _addr_pkey;
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because `_dummy_bnd` and `_dummy_pkey` are defined as `short`, which does not meet the pointer alignment requirements of the union. This misalignment causes the offset of `si_pkey` to be incorrect, leading to potential issues in signal handling.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
struct {
    compat_uptr_t _dummy_bnd;
    compat_uptr_t _lower;
    compat_uptr_t _upper;
} _sigfault;
```
```c
struct {
    compat_uptr_t _dummy_pkey;
    u32 _pkey;
} _addr_pkey;
```
Reason:
The fix changes `_dummy_bnd` and `_dummy_pkey` to `compat_uptr_t`, which is a pointer type. This adjustment ensures proper alignment of the union, thereby correcting the offset of `si_pkey` and ensuring that signal handling functions correctly for memory access violations.

